    title: "THE PARTY",
    gamesTitle: "GAMELAR RO'YXATI",
    textHtml: `<h3>The Party</h3><p>Cody's family moved to a new house. His dad got a new job as a <span class="keyword-tooltip" data-tooltip="professor">professor</span>. Cody liked his new town, but he missed his grandparents. For his birthday, Cody wanted to have a party. His dad said, “Yes, we could even have a <span class="keyword-tooltip" data-tooltip="guruh">band</span> play!”</p><p>On the day of the party, Cody woke up and <span class="keyword-tooltip" data-tooltip="yelmoq; shoshmoq">rushed</span> to get ready. He started to check his <span class="keyword-tooltip" data-tooltip="ro'yxat">list</span> of things to do. He was so excited! But then he <span class="keyword-tooltip" data-tooltip="payqamoq, sezmoq">noticed</span> something terrible. There was snow on the ground and lots of it! “Dad!” he yelled. “How can the band play their <span class="keyword-tooltip" data-tooltip="asbob">instruments</span> outside?”</p><p>Dad said, “We’ll move the <span class="keyword-tooltip" data-tooltip="sahna">stage</span> inside.” It <span class="keyword-tooltip" data-tooltip="arang; sal-pal">barely</span> fit <span class="keyword-tooltip" data-tooltip="ichida">within</span> the garage because there were some boxes and <span class="keyword-tooltip" data-tooltip="chiqindi, axlat">garbage</span> there. But when they finished, they got a call from the band. They did not want to come in the snow <span class="keyword-tooltip" data-tooltip="bo'ron, to'fon">storm</span>.</p><p>Dad said, “Let’s get someone to perform <span class="keyword-tooltip" data-tooltip="sehr, jodu">magic</span>.” But no one would come because of the snow.</p><p>Finally, Dad said, “Cody, there’s too much snow. We need to <span class="keyword-tooltip" data-tooltip="bekor qilmoq">cancel</span> the party.”</p><p>“Yes, sir,” Cody said sadly. “It’s going to be a <span class="keyword-tooltip" data-tooltip="zerikarli">boring</span> birthday,” he <span class="keyword-tooltip" data-tooltip="bashorat qilmoq, oldindan aytmoq">predicted</span>. Cody wanted to <span class="keyword-tooltip" data-tooltip="bo'lishmoq, baham ko'rmoq">share</span> his birthday with someone. He wanted to be at his old home. He wanted to see his grandparents.</p><p>But then something got his attention. He noticed a car in the <span class="keyword-tooltip" data-tooltip="tratuar, yo'lak">driveway</span>. His grandparents <span class="keyword-tooltip" data-tooltip="egalik qilmoq">owned</span> a car like that!</p><p>Cody was right. His grandparents came for his birthday! “Happy birthday, Cody! We’re sorry we are late. But there was so much snow. It made us go off <span class="keyword-tooltip" data-tooltip="jadval">schedule</span>. We tried to leave a <span class="keyword-tooltip" data-tooltip="xabar">message</span> to tell you.”</p><p>Cody told them what happened. “I’m sorry,” said Grandpa.</p><p>“I was sad,” Cody said. “But I’m not anymore. I’m so happy to see you.” Dad brought out Cody's birthday treat. It was his favorite type, a sundae with whipped cream on top. Then Cody told his grandparents about the new town. It was his best birthday ever.</p>`,
